oogle Scholar\", \"snowball\", \"reasoning\", \"acting\", \"interacting\". But I need continuous quotes of 20+ chars supporting answers. I'll print those lines with surrounding context.\n\nLet's do it.\n\nCareful: I must include a proper ```python block. Let's write:\n\n```python\nimport json\nr = run_command([\"python\",\"read_pdf.py\",\"--start-page\",\"4\",\"--end-page\",\"5\"])\nd = json.loads(r['stdout'])\nfor p in d['pages']:\n    for ln in p['text'].split('\\n'):\n        if any(k in ln.lower() for k in ['categor','google scholar','snowball','reasoning','acting','interacting','literature']):\n            print(p['page'],'|',ln)\n```\n\nThat prints matched lines; but quote needs continuous original text. Matched lines are individual lines; a quote can span multiple consecutive lines if I reconstruct. Risky but acceptable if I print the full paragraph. Better: print full page text for p.4-5? Too long maybe (each page ~3000 chars, 2 pages 6000). That's fine within budget.\n\nActually printing 2 pages ~6000 chars is acceptable. Let's print full text of pages 4,5 (truncate to 3000 each maybe). Let's just print.\n\nBut budget: 11 requests left per harness. Hmm, \"requests_left\":11 counts my actions apparently. I need report write + pytest + final answer. So maybe 4-5 actions for reading max.\n\nCombine: one action can do multiple run_command calls! Yes — group independent operations in one action. So one action: read_pdf pages 4-5, 10, 13, 23, 45, 47, 52 via several run_command calls, and print filtered lines from each. That's a single request from my side.\n\nLet's do that with keyword-filtered printing, plus print context lines around matches. I'll print whole pages for critical ones but they may be large... total maybe 20k chars. Should be OK-ish but let's filter smartly: for each page, print lines containing keywords plus the following 2 lines.\n\nActually exact quotes matter. Safer to print full relevant paragraphs. Let me print full text of pages 4,5,10,13 (4 pages ~12k chars) — a lot. Hmm.\n\nCompromise: print full text of pages 4, 5 (need categories + search methods), page 10 (self consistency), page 13 (ToT), page 23 (Toolformer/ToolBench), page 45 (CAMEL), page 47 (Generative agents), page 52 (conclusion). That's 8 pages, maybe 25k chars. Too much but manageable? Risky for budget.\n\nUse keyword filter with window: for each page, find lines with keywords and print ±2 lines.\n\nLet me craft keywords per page.\n\nI'll do it."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8158,"completion_tokens":2517,"total_tokens":10675,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4352},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2052},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4352,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":3806},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}